<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32804" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπῠρ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>burn to ashes, consume utterly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1070
			</span></i>(lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HF</u>
					421
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>set on fire,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				341a18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>catch fire,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				342b2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				19.3
			</span></i> : a term used in the Stoic philos. to express <i>the
				tendency</i> of all things <i>to pass into fire,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Zeno Stoic.
				2.182
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be burnt up,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμπάσιν κεραυνίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					244
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>to be much heated,</i> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.25
			</span></i>, f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Aph.</u>
				7.38
			</span></i> ; <i>to become red-hot,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				12.25.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>heat, warm,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαλανεῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					1.16
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
